"Conan!" you whisper urgently, "the rifle...shoot!"

Trembling with fear, Conan takes his father's double-barrelled rifle and points it at the beast... And at that moment, it occurs to you that it might not be so easy to kill the predator. Maybe it's better to scare him off?

"Wait, don't shoot at him, shoot in the air!"

In another situation, Conan would probably argue, but now he is too scared. A shot rings out. The beast snorts abruptly and steps back.

"Shoot again, from the other barrel! Shoo, dog, buzz off, A-A-A-A!"

Conan shoots once again. You can hear the screams of animals, running away deeper into the forest. You shout as loudly as possible, advancing towards the predator. And just when you think that you are done for, the beast wavers. Its frightful burning eyes vanish into the thicket, and a ringing silence falls upon the glade.